WEBVTT

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.230
I know where you belong...

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.430
And it's with us.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.740
You're like me...

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.390
You have black rocks coming out of you.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.250
You're the guy who lent me 
a Kitetsu Blade this morning, right?

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.040
Are you crying?

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.110
Sorry... I'm just so happy I found you.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.470
When we first met, I had a suspicion, but...

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.810
It was really you after all.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.560
I've wanted to meet you
 for the longest time!

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.190
Oh, don't mind me. 
I'm talking to the one inside of you.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.900
The one inside of me...?

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.990
I mean these black stones.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:48.050
They're why you can't use 
Kitetsu Blades, right?

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.170
I was the same way.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.640
The people you share your dreams
 with leave you in the dust.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.240
But how could you argue?

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.610
Because you can't fight on your own.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.270
You don't want that to be the end, right?

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.630
You want to get strong
 and catch up to them, right?

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.190
Yeah.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.100
You're exactly right.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:13.750
So, is there a way for us to get stronger?

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:16.250
You bet.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.980
<b>The
Obsidian
Goddess</b>

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.820
What do I have to do to use a Kitetsu Blade?

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.520
You just need to accept the black stones.

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:57.850
I have to accept them?

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.060
Yep.

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:03.480
A haze came over you during your trial 
 and you blacked out, right?

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:08.190
You just need to surrender yourself
to that feeling and let it take you!

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.050
You'll become strong if you do!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.250
How strong are we talking?

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.180
Strong enough...

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:19.710
to do <i>this</i>.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:45.860
What the?!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.680
Where'd that huge pit come from?

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:56.880
That guy in black cut it 
open with a single sword!

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.450
What?! That can't be!

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.320
<i>This guy is crazy.</i>

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.750
Wait, did that power not come 
from your Kitetsu Blade?

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:13.560
Go on, take the sword's trial.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.520
Then you can become a 
Kitetsu Blade yourself!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.870
<i>Become</i> a Kitetsu Blade?

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.430
What are you talking about?

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:24.040
I thought I was gonna be able 
to wield them like you!

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.830
Not what I meant!

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.790
You're going to <i>be</i> a Kitetsu Blade.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.280
Didn't I just show you 
how strong you'd become?

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.920
Then you meant... No way!

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.530
That's right! You're a rare find!

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:41.660
With those black stones, you could 
become the ultimate Kitetsu Blade!

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.450
What's with you?

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.910
You think I can turn into a sword?

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.870
Are you serious?

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.030
Are you sure <i>you're</i> serious?

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.110
I thought you wanted to be the strongest.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.600
And you can!

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.510
What difference does it make 
if you're a human or a sword?!

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.900
The answer's obviously no.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.820
I won't be able to fight alongside 
Kojiro and Tsugumi if I do that!

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.420
I see.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.320
Then what should we do?

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.320
Okay, we'll turn your friends 
into material for my swords, too!

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.660
You won't be lonely then, right?!

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:22.090
The Bushi are heading up 
that mountain, aren't they?

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:24.570
Hey! What do you think you're—

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.940
Into the forge go the raw materials.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.330
Keep moving up the mountain!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.920
The Kishin is at the peak!

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:49.870
Kojiro! Kojiro, we don't have to rush!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.860
If we're not fast, 
the Bushi bands will slay the Kishin.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:57.880
Ugh! Why are you suddenly 
so fired up about this?

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:02.390
And are you sure it was a good idea to 
leave Musashi when he's feeling down?

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.810
Isn't that kind of cold?

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:08.100
It's fine.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:11.920
What could we do for him 
right now if we'd stayed?

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.040
Try and cheer him up by saying,

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.590
"I can use Kitetsu Blades, 
and I'm sure you can too someday"?

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:20.480
That'd only make it harder for him.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.590
So I'm going to go on ahead,

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.930
figure out this Kishin's weakness,

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:29.950
and wait for Musashi to get back on his feet!

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.070
Will he be able to, though?

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:36.150
What?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.410
Remember what the lady said?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.560
That black aura means he 
can't use Kitetsu Blades...

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:42.140
And it's really rare.

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.240
Just who is Musashi really?

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:49.310
I mean, if he's really one of 
these legendary forsaken...

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.180
He can't be normal.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:55.110
That got me thinking...

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:59.520
Musashi's probably inherited some 
kind of amazing power, right?

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.400
Maybe he's from a special family.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.800
You've gotta tell me! 
We're friends, aren't we?

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.240
I guess you're right.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:14.480
Where do I begin?

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:21.210
When it comes to Musashi's family...

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:27.120
There was a massive mountain
with a mine in Tatsuyama.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:32.950
And at the foot of it were 
homes, shops, and schools.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:38.650
And beyond that, there was 
an incredibly massive...

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.690
...field. They were farmers.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:49.170
Farmers?

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:50.530
Farmers.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:52.740
Are you messing with me?!

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.860
I wasn't trying to!

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:59.080
He's from a family of farmers, 
like most everyone in Tatsuyama.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.920
Is that all? Disappointing.

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:08.250
As for me, I was the child 
of the last Bushi in Tatsuyama.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:12.710
We lived in a bamboo grove
 on the edge of town.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.680
Being Bushi, the descendants of criminals,

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.130
meant everybody kept their distance.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.140
But Musashi was a weird kid.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.440
A katana made you a target 
for prejudice in town.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.160
But he...

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.700
That...

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:46.700
was super cool!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.850
How'd you cut that leaf?!

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.190
Come on, how'd you do it?!
You gotta tell me!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.750
Uh... l-like this!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.620
Like this?

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.210
Huh, didn't work.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:10.810
It was so awesome, though! I wanna do it!

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:13.500
<i>He said it was awesome...</i>

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.060
I'd never been praised like that before.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:21.600
Musashi didn't treat me differently.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:27.860
Just having a real friend like him 
made me happier than I ever imagined.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:30.300
Hey!

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:33.050
And thanks to that weirdo of a friend,

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.500
my life wasn't a total nightmare.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.480
I'm glad.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:39.500
Yeah.

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:45.690
But if everyone in your town 
hated Bushi, why didn't Musashi?

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:49.140
Probably because of his parents.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.640
They were pretty odd, too.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.470
They never cared what other people said.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.650
They treated my dad and I well.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.880
It was a shame when they got sick and died.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.510
They were really nice.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:06.110
What is it?

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:09.160
This just makes it harder to understand.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:13.410
You're saying Musashi and his parents
were all totally normal people, right?

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:14.080
What of it?

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:18.410
So why do Kitetsu Blades 
scorn him the way they do?

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:24.150
If we don't understand that, 
we can't help him find a way around it.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.340
Well...

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:35.430
Is he really going to make his way back to us?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.940
Now then, let's see how this goes.

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:44.050
Master.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:46.300
Hey, Nanao.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.330
<b>Inukai
Shiro
of the
???
Band</b>

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.540
I brought lunch.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.290
Please be grateful.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.010
<b>Inukai
Nanao
of the
???
Band</b>

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:59.180
Hey, great job! 
This is gonna be a real feast.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:02.300
Huh. What happened to the redhead?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.730
Oh, I threw him in the pit.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.010
I see.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:09.630
Huh? Why do you look so sad?

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.600
He was kind to me.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.640
I was hoping to talk to him.

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.750
That's a real shame.

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:22.990
I'm not sure you know 
the meaning of the word "shame."

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:28.620
You probably fed him what he wanted 
to hear to get close to him, didn't you?

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:33.950
"I'm also a black-stone forsaken.
I understand how you feel."

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.140
Which is all a lie, isn't it?

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:40.800
You're the one person I'd never lie to.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.020
You really are a sophist devil.

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:47.580
The only thing you're earnest 
about is Kitetsu Blades...

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:50.990
And you've finally found her
inside of that redhead, right?

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:51.970
Your goddess.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:53.930
I have.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.820
The Obsidian Goddess that 
I've been searching for.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.980
Are you sure it's really her?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.870
Not another fake?

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.320
This time I'm sure it's really her.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.950
Then why not just collect her already?

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.820
This all seems rather circuitous, Master.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:15.780
Nanao, my dear, wasted time 
is what makes for a fulfilling life.

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:17.790
I prefer to do things efficiently.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:21.380
I'm after some black stone.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.670
Gonna head out for a bit.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.330
Keep an eye on things here, Nanao.

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:35.020
I see... Master intends on using
that boy as material for a sword.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.250
In that case, I feel sorry for him.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.900
He'll be forced to make a terrible 
decision at the bottom of the abyss.

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:47.820
<i>I keep falling.</i>

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.670
<i>And I've lost track of time.</i>

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.160
<i>But I'm not...</i>

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.160
<i>gonna hit rock bottom without a fight!</i>

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:05.640
<i>I've gotta do </i>something<i>! 
There has to be a way!</i>

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:10.170
<i>That's it!</i>

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:21.540
I've stopped. What a relief.

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:26.070
But what's this blade doing down here?

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.470
He can let go of the sword 
and be burned alive.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:45.660
Or he can let go of his consciousness 
and turn into black stone.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:49.360
Either way, he's not making it back alive.

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:55.750
Dammit, my body feels so heavy... 
My head's foggy too...

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:59.030
It's just like during my sword trial.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.530
What do I do?

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:08.210
Ow!

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:11.370
That was close. I almost passed out.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:15.180
But I just have to stay awake, right?

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:20.080
And these black stones are perfect 
for getting out of this hole.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.280
Okay. I'm gonna climb my way outta here.

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:26.610
I'm afraid I can't allow that. 
You must hide for now.

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:27.970
Wh-Who's there?!

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:46.770
This is...

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:52.540
You should stay here with me forever.

00:14:55.880 --> 00:14:58.890
No... You've gotta let me out.

00:14:59.270 --> 00:15:01.050
My friends need my help!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.870
You won't be able to do 
anything even if you go.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.320
You don't have the strength to fight.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.010
You would only get in the way.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:13.980
I still have to go back, though.

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:24.100
I told you they don't need you.

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:26.810
It's the same as before, remember?

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.040
You do remember, don't you?

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:30.630
Remember.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.970
Remember...

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:40.960
This is...

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:45.480
Mom, wake up...

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:46.540
Huh?

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.790
Even if it was an epidemic, 
for so many to die...

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.580
It's because they didn't have 
enough faith in our oni masters.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:55.840
Divine punishment for 
their blasphemous ways.

00:15:55.840 --> 00:15:57.760
You know how that one couple used to act.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:01.580
What's going to happen with their son now?

00:16:01.580 --> 00:16:05.220
Good question. Town laws say that it's 
up to his relatives to take him in.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.970
No one wants a child like him.

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:13.110
I'm don't see why we have 
to take care of you.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.780
B-But... they... um...

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:18.420
Oh, would you shut up? And get lost!

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.220
Don't ever come back!

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:25.630
Uncle, Auntie, thank you 
for letting me stay.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.490
I'll help a whole bunch.

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:31.240
I'll chop wood, or clean the well, or—

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:35.230
There's one condition for you to 
become a part of this family.

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.100
Anything you want!

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.050
Don't do anything.

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.480
Taking in the child of faithless parents
 who showed mercy to Bushi

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.240
will look terrible to others.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:48.150
You need to draw as little attention 
as possible. Understood?

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.090
O-Okay...

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:56.570
But, um, what's so bad about being 
friends with Kojiro and Pops?

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.270
This little idiot doesn't 
understand a damn thing!

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:07.530
This is what you get 
with blasphemers for parents!

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:11.290
<i>I better not keep talking about the 
Kanemakis around other people.</i>

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.890
<i>Being friends with Bushi 
will get me in trouble...</i>

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:17.110
Listen up. You don't leave the 
house without permission.

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:19.600
In town, you don't talk to us at all.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:20.290
Y-Yes, sir!

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.280
Don't talk!

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:25.010
You don't have to respond, either, okay?

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.060
Good morning.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.750
Come on, get out of bed.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:37.550
What's for breakfast?

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:50.080
Uncle!

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:00.540
Hey, is that the boy you took in?

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:03.500
The son of the blasphemers?

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:06.220
I can't believe you're 
actually taking care of him.

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:10.240
How many times did I tell you to stay 
away from us around other people?!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:14.240
He's wasted enough of our time. 
Come on, let's enjoy our meal.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:16.700
Come on, dear. I can't wait to dig in.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.700
Let's eat while it's hot.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:28.230
<i>It feels kind of like I'm a ghost...</i>

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:31.270
<i>No one calls my name.</i>

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.040
<i>Or pays me any attention. Or smiles at me.</i>

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.090
<i>I've figured something out.</i>

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.020
<i>If no one in the world cares about you...</i>

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.960
<i>it's no different from being dead.</i>

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:48.960
<i>I guess just breathing isn't 
the same thing as being alive.</i>

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:55.180
<i>I want...</i>

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:57.910
<i>I want someone to see me.</i>

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.760
<i>I want to be of use to someone!</i>

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:03.470
<i>I want someone to like me!</i>

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:06.520
<i>But... But who...?</i>

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:09.850
<i>Kojiro... Pops...</i>

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.140
<i>I wish I could see them.</i>

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:13.860
Hey.

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:17.270
I have something for you to do.

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:19.870
I'll do anything!

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:21.710
I want to be useful to you and the others!

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:24.180
Throw this rock at him.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:29.600
Everyone will think better of you.

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:33.970
Prove that you're not like your parents.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:36.430
Go on. Do it.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:37.870
Do it.

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:38.600
Do it.

00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:38.960
Do it.

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:39.200
Do it.

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.090
Do it.

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:40.950
Do it.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:41.540
Do it.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:41.880
Do it.

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:42.430
Do it.

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.100
Do it.

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:43.640
Do it.

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:44.290
Do it.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:44.450
Do it.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.040
Do it.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:45.700
Do it.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.120
Do it.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:46.920
Do it.

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.310
Do it.

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:48.060
Do it.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:48.700
Do it.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:49.200
Do it.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.480
Do it!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.250
Do it!

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.100
Do it!

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:57.060
Do it!

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.040
Do it!

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:00.050
Do it!

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:13.910
The remaining Bushi... should just die.

00:20:15.530 --> 00:20:17.990
That's right! Listen to the kid!

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.560
Go to hell, Bushi!

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:23.020
Musashi...

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:27.840
You threw the rock in that moment.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:32.790
Because no one needed you...

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:36.750
You were willing to do whatever 
it took to feel wanted.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.010
Anything at all.

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:39.870
That's who you are.

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:42.720
You say you want to be a Bushi,

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:46.290
but that's just an excuse to be 
with your friend, isn't it?

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:49.510
Okay, we're gonna do it too, Kojiro!

00:20:49.820 --> 00:20:52.710
I'm happy as long as we can 
chase our dream together.

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:56.070
I wish I could have joined him.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:03.110
To you, being a Bushi and wielding a 
katana are simply a means to an end,

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:05.780
no different than the rock 
you threw that day.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:09.570
There's no way someone like 
that can use a Kitetsu Blade.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:14.280
And if you can't fight, then you're 
of no value to your friends.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.450
You'll have to forgive me.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:21.780
The only way to break your will to fight was 
to revisit these memories from your past.

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:26.320
If you were to leave this place and 
start fighting, they could capture me.

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:30.620
Because you are I one, in body and soul.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:34.020
So let's hide here forever.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:41.310
You don't need to involve yourself 
in the war between Bushi and oni.

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:53.770
This thing is a Kishin?

00:23:25.460 --> 00:23:26.670
Nanao!

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:27.960
What is it?

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.640
I wanted to show my gratitude for 
your help in my Kitetsu Blade search.

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:31.710
This is for you!

00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:33.250
Master...!

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:34.510
<b>Beeeam</b>

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:34.490
I stole it, by the way.

00:23:34.490 --> 00:23:36.390
You just say whatever you want, don't you?!

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:38.210
Sophist devil!

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Next Time
A Bushi's Way of Life</b>
